    "A WIN THAT DID NOT END THE DEBATE — Schumer's supporters argue that the election results show he can organize a winning coalition. Senator Kirsten Gillibrand, who led Democrats' Senate campaign operation, has defended his role in winning back the chamber. Others argue that electoral success does not answer how aggressively Democrats should use their new majority.",
